1
00:00:02,396 --> 00:00:03,396
Good morning.

2
00:00:07,187 --> 00:00:09,895
(groaning)

3
00:00:09,979 --> 00:00:12,937
(atmospheric music)

4
00:00:21,854 --> 00:00:24,477
So which one of the
two are you right now?

5
00:00:25,561 --> 00:00:28,477
Hey wait. Aren't you...

6
00:00:28,561 --> 00:00:29,477
Satoru Gojou.

7
00:00:29,561 --> 00:00:32,102
I'm head of the
first-years at Jujutsu Tech.

8
00:00:33,769 --> 00:00:34,769
Jujutsu?

9
00:00:34,811 --> 00:00:36,227
Fushiguro!

10
00:00:36,311 --> 00:00:37,227
Where is he-

11
00:00:37,311 --> 00:00:39,311
-(ropes tensing)
-Huh?

12
00:00:39,394 --> 00:00:41,476
(distressing music)

13
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:43,810
What the hell is this?

14
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:47,286
I wouldn't be worrying
about others right now...

15
00:00:47,310 --> 00:00:49,393
Yuuji Itadori.

16
00:00:49,476 --> 00:00:50,184
(gasps)

17
00:00:50,268 --> 00:00:52,560
You see, it's been decided

18
00:00:52,643 --> 00:00:55,560
that you're to be
secretly executed.

19
00:00:55,643 --> 00:00:58,392
(Opening Theme Music)

20
00:01:13,975 --> 00:01:17,725
(singing in Japanese)

21
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:27,220
(phone ringing)

22
00:02:29,429 --> 00:02:30,345
[Nurse] Sugisawa Hospital.

23
00:02:30,429 --> 00:02:31,178
This is Yuuji Itadori.

24
00:02:31,262 --> 00:02:33,845
I just called earlier.

25
00:02:33,928 --> 00:02:35,012
Yes.

26
00:02:35,094 --> 00:02:36,136
Yes.

27
00:02:36,219 --> 00:02:37,803
I'm sorry to
keep calling, but...

28
00:02:37,886 --> 00:02:39,469
how's my grandpa doing?

29
00:02:39,553 --> 00:02:42,594
[Nurse] Huh? I thought
they already told you.

30
00:02:42,678 --> 00:02:43,594
Oh, never mind.

31
00:02:43,678 --> 00:02:46,094
Just hold on a minute.
I'll go find out myself.

32
00:02:46,177 --> 00:02:49,427
(soft guitar music)

33
00:02:49,510 --> 00:02:51,468
Mister Itadori never
uses his call button.

34
00:02:51,552 --> 00:02:53,343
It's kinda scary
that he doesn't.

35
00:02:54,677 --> 00:02:55,468
[Nurse] Mister
Itadori, you have a call.

36
00:02:55,552 --> 00:02:56,468
It's your grandson again,

37
00:02:56,552 --> 00:02:58,218
asking if you want
him to bring you any-

38
00:02:58,302 --> 00:03:00,218
Leave me alone!!

39
00:03:00,302 --> 00:03:01,844
Tell him not to come here!

40
00:03:01,927 --> 00:03:03,467
-(gasps)
-He should go to his club!

41
00:03:03,551 --> 00:03:04,551
Go to his club!

42
00:03:05,426 --> 00:03:06,342
[Nurse] I, uh...

43
00:03:06,426 --> 00:03:09,467
I guess you probably heard that.

44
00:03:09,551 --> 00:03:11,384
So what type club
are you in, Yuuji?

45
00:03:13,092 --> 00:03:14,884
Yeah. I heard.

46
00:03:14,968 --> 00:03:15,968
Thanks a lot.

47
00:03:18,301 --> 00:03:19,300
(footsteps)

48
00:03:19,383 --> 00:03:20,842
(dog barking)

49
00:03:20,925 --> 00:03:23,050
(sirens)

50
00:03:30,967 --> 00:03:32,317
They're keeping a
cursed object here,

51
00:03:32,341 --> 00:03:33,883
in a place like this?

52
00:03:33,967 --> 00:03:35,465
Could they be any more stupid?

53
00:03:38,799 --> 00:03:41,716
(hutch door creaking)

54
00:03:41,799 --> 00:03:42,716
Huh?

55
00:03:42,799 --> 00:03:44,882
(groans)

56
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:48,507
There's nothing here.

57
00:03:48,590 --> 00:03:49,507
[Satoru Gojou] Huh?

58
00:03:49,590 --> 00:03:51,381
The Stevenson hutch is empty.

59
00:03:51,464 --> 00:03:53,506
[Satoru] For real?
That's hilarious!

60
00:03:53,589 --> 00:03:56,048
Maybe it took a
nighttime stroll.

61
00:03:56,131 --> 00:03:57,256
I'm going to punch you.

62
00:03:57,339 --> 00:04:00,339
[Satoru] Well, no going
home until it's recovered, okay?

63
00:04:00,423 --> 00:04:01,423
(call disconnects)

64
00:04:03,256 --> 00:04:04,923
I'm seriously
going to punch him.

65
00:04:07,755 --> 00:04:10,714
(chattering)

66
00:04:10,797 --> 00:04:13,297
Ready to go? What do you say?

67
00:04:13,630 --> 00:04:14,547
Sasaki?

68
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:15,547
(grunts)

69
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:16,547
Iguchi?

70
00:04:16,630 --> 00:04:17,547
(grunts)

71
00:04:17,630 --> 00:04:19,547
Okay...

72
00:04:19,630 --> 00:04:20,714
go!

73
00:04:20,797 --> 00:04:21,964
Spirit gods, spirit gods,

74
00:04:22,047 --> 00:04:25,005
which creature is the council
president barely weaker than?

75
00:04:25,504 --> 00:04:26,421
(gasps)

76
00:04:26,504 --> 00:04:27,421
[All Three] Ku..

77
00:04:27,504 --> 00:04:28,421
ri...

78
00:04:28,504 --> 00:04:30,629
o... ne.

79
00:04:30,713 --> 00:04:33,296
-A sea angel's tougher?
-(laughing)

80
00:04:33,379 --> 00:04:34,754
Occult club!

81
00:04:34,838 --> 00:04:35,754
Hey!

82
00:04:35,838 --> 00:04:37,462
Plankton president. What's up?

83
00:04:37,546 --> 00:04:38,587
(slams)

84
00:04:38,671 --> 00:04:40,128
As you were previously informed,

85
00:04:40,211 --> 00:04:41,753
a research club
with no real activities

86
00:04:41,837 --> 00:04:43,378
must forfeit its club room.

87
00:04:43,461 --> 00:04:45,086
So vacate now!

88
00:04:45,169 --> 00:04:46,753
You really ought
to be more careful

89
00:04:46,837 --> 00:04:49,004
not to underestimate
our members, President.

90
00:04:49,461 --> 00:04:51,962
(slams)

91
00:04:52,086 --> 00:04:53,169
And what is that?

92
00:04:53,503 --> 00:04:56,003
You know about the
school's rugby field

93
00:04:56,085 --> 00:04:57,460
being closed off, don't you?

94
00:04:57,544 --> 00:04:58,460
[School President] Yes.

95
00:04:58,544 --> 00:04:59,335
Some of the
students who got sick

96
00:04:59,419 --> 00:05:01,794
actually had to be hospitalized.

97
00:05:01,877 --> 00:05:03,419
And so you don't
find that alarming?

98
00:05:03,502 --> 00:05:06,752
We're talking about some
tough rugby players here!

99
00:05:06,836 --> 00:05:07,836
The players said that,

100
00:05:07,877 --> 00:05:08,502
just before they
started feeling sick...

101
00:05:08,585 --> 00:05:09,502
(bong)

102
00:05:09,585 --> 00:05:10,502
(gasps)

103
00:05:10,585 --> 00:05:12,793
they heard mysterious
sounds and voices

104
00:05:12,876 --> 00:05:13,960
coming from the field!

105
00:05:14,043 --> 00:05:16,584
And then we found this
newspaper article from 30 years ago.

106
00:05:16,668 --> 00:05:18,626
It talks about the disappearance

107
00:05:18,710 --> 00:05:20,043
of a certain Mister Yoshida,

108
00:05:20,126 --> 00:05:21,751
who worked for the
construction company.

109
00:05:21,835 --> 00:05:23,334
It says he was last sighted here

110
00:05:23,418 --> 00:05:25,394
at Sugisawa Third High
School during its construction.

111
00:05:25,418 --> 00:05:26,334
(groans)

112
00:05:26,418 --> 00:05:28,959
Yoshida was struggling
to make ends meet,

113
00:05:29,042 --> 00:05:29,834
so he turned to loan sharks,

114
00:05:29,917 --> 00:05:32,333
and those organizations
were after him!

115
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:36,834
Which means the whole
mysterious disaster at the rugby field

116
00:05:36,917 --> 00:05:38,834
was caused by the
vengeful spirit of Yoshida,

117
00:05:38,917 --> 00:05:40,375
whose body is buried there!

118
00:05:40,458 --> 00:05:43,541
No, actually it was just ticks.

119
00:05:43,624 --> 00:05:44,666
(light percussive music)

120
00:05:44,749 --> 00:05:47,833
Hard ticks, to be exact.
Large blood-sucking bugs.

121
00:05:47,916 --> 00:05:50,041
If one bites you and
infects you with SFTS,

122
00:05:50,124 --> 00:05:51,684
it can be fatal, so
you have to be careful.

123
00:05:51,708 --> 00:05:54,249
So what if it was ticks?

124
00:05:54,332 --> 00:05:55,558
The occult club is trying
to uncover occult activity

125
00:05:55,582 --> 00:05:57,374
so it's still a valid
activity report!

126
00:05:57,457 --> 00:05:59,623
This is not some
kind of kids' game!

127
00:05:59,707 --> 00:06:02,623
Besides the biggest
problem is you, Yuuji Itadori!

128
00:06:02,707 --> 00:06:06,206
You're registered with track
and field, not the occult club!

129
00:06:06,290 --> 00:06:07,516
So this club doesn't even
have the three members

130
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:10,248
required to be a club!

131
00:06:10,331 --> 00:06:11,331
Uh...

132
00:06:11,373 --> 00:06:11,623
You did that?

133
00:06:11,707 --> 00:06:12,623
But I...

134
00:06:12,707 --> 00:06:14,998
I'm sure I wrote "occult club"!

135
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,872
I'm the one who changed it.

136
00:06:16,956 --> 00:06:19,205
Coach Takagi? What for?

137
00:06:19,289 --> 00:06:22,247
Because! The track and
field team needs you on it!

138
00:06:22,330 --> 00:06:23,932
[School President] So
says the only teacher

139
00:06:23,956 --> 00:06:25,706
more problematic
than the students.

140
00:06:25,789 --> 00:06:27,872
How many times
do I have to tell you

141
00:06:27,956 --> 00:06:29,205
I'm not joining the team?

142
00:06:29,289 --> 00:06:31,038
-You are.
-No I'm not!

143
00:06:31,121 --> 00:06:32,579
However I'm not some demon.

144
00:06:32,663 --> 00:06:35,496
So if you can defeat me I'll
excuse you from the team.

145
00:06:35,579 --> 00:06:39,038
And we'll settle this fair
and square by competing!

146
00:06:39,121 --> 00:06:42,079
That'll work! You've got a deal!

147
00:06:42,162 --> 00:06:43,162
-Yay!
-Yay!

148
00:06:43,663 --> 00:06:45,496
[School President]
How fair and square is it

149
00:06:45,579 --> 00:06:47,495
to re-write a student's
club application?

150
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:52,704
(birds whistling)

151
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:55,495
[Fushiguro] What's
with this rugby field?

152
00:06:55,578 --> 00:06:57,578
(gurgling)

153
00:06:57,662 --> 00:07:00,078
Is there a dead body
buried here or something?

154
00:07:01,161 --> 00:07:03,703
Even if there is, I'm
surprised to see a cursed spirit

155
00:07:03,786 --> 00:07:05,077
this high-level here.

156
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:07,077
That looks like a
grade-two curse.

157
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:09,119
Must be the influence
of that cursed object.

158
00:07:09,202 --> 00:07:11,911
(growling)

159
00:07:11,995 --> 00:07:15,077
Damn. Its presence is
too strong to pin down.

160
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:16,536
It feels like it's close by,

161
00:07:16,619 --> 00:07:17,939
but it could
actually be far away.

162
00:07:19,952 --> 00:07:22,660
This special-grade cursed
object's a serious pain.

163
00:07:23,952 --> 00:07:26,660
Who could have moved
it? And where is it now?

164
00:07:27,702 --> 00:07:29,535
[Male Student] Hey,
come here, check this out!

165
00:07:29,618 --> 00:07:33,118
Coach Takagi is taking on
Itadori from West Middle!

166
00:07:33,201 --> 00:07:35,080
[Male Student] Wow, what
are they competing for?

167
00:07:35,784 --> 00:07:37,450
[Takagi] Yeah!

168
00:07:38,158 --> 00:07:39,158
(grunt)

169
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:39,909
14 meters!

170
00:07:39,993 --> 00:07:40,742
-(victorious music)
-(grunting)

171
00:07:40,826 --> 00:07:42,784
(applause and cheering)

172
00:07:42,867 --> 00:07:46,284
[Man] Wow,
Takagi's still got it!

173
00:07:46,367 --> 00:07:48,034
Wow, is he famous or something?

174
00:07:48,117 --> 00:07:50,783
It's just a rumor, but
I heard that he beat

175
00:07:50,866 --> 00:07:52,408
all the stages of
"Ninja Warrior"

176
00:07:52,491 --> 00:07:54,741
and that he's the
reincarnation of Mirko Cro Cop.

177
00:07:54,825 --> 00:07:56,616
[Sasaki] But Mirko's
not even dead yet.

178
00:07:56,700 --> 00:08:00,116
He earned the nickname
"Tiger of West Middle."

179
00:08:00,199 --> 00:08:01,116
That's lame.

180
00:08:01,199 --> 00:08:03,283
Hey, so can I throw
it however I want?

181
00:08:03,366 --> 00:08:04,408
Mm-hm!

182
00:08:04,491 --> 00:08:06,573
For this challenge you can
throw however you want.

183
00:08:06,657 --> 00:08:09,949
After all, I know this
event isn't your strong suit.

184
00:08:10,032 --> 00:08:12,490
You've probably
never even really been...

185
00:08:12,573 --> 00:08:14,532
(crash)

186
00:08:16,032 --> 00:08:16,949
Uh...

187
00:08:17,032 --> 00:08:18,407
about 30 meters, I guess.

188
00:08:18,490 --> 00:08:19,407
(crowd gasps)

189
00:08:19,490 --> 00:08:21,824
Yes! I crushed it!

190
00:08:21,907 --> 00:08:24,155
Kinda more gorilla than tiger.

191
00:08:24,239 --> 00:08:26,447
He threw that like a pitcher!

192
00:08:26,531 --> 00:08:28,614
You'd do really well on
a sports team, Itadori.

193
00:08:28,698 --> 00:08:29,990
(crowd chattering)

194
00:08:30,072 --> 00:08:32,322
Don't force yourself to
stay in our occult club.

195
00:08:32,406 --> 00:08:33,489
Huh?

196
00:08:33,572 --> 00:08:34,322
Really?

197
00:08:34,406 --> 00:08:36,239
But even though
you love scary stuff

198
00:08:36,322 --> 00:08:38,822
without me you could
never go to haunted places!

199
00:08:38,905 --> 00:08:40,822
But we like being scared.

200
00:08:40,905 --> 00:08:43,321
School rules are I
have to be in some club.

201
00:08:43,405 --> 00:08:44,989
And I could never keep this up.

202
00:08:45,071 --> 00:08:47,822
You don't have to do anything!
You can be a ghost member!

203
00:08:47,905 --> 00:08:49,446
After all we're the occult club!

204
00:08:49,530 --> 00:08:50,446
(chuckles)

205
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:51,989
Yeah I did say that.

206
00:08:52,071 --> 00:08:55,195
Besides, I want to be
able to go home by 6:00.

207
00:08:55,279 --> 00:08:57,153
So if you two
don't mind I'll stay.

208
00:08:57,237 --> 00:08:59,654
I really like being in your
club. It has a great vibe.

209
00:08:59,737 --> 00:09:02,821
Well in that case we're
happy to have you back.

210
00:09:02,904 --> 00:09:03,904
Yeah.

211
00:09:03,946 --> 00:09:05,195
(laughing)

212
00:09:05,279 --> 00:09:06,380
[Fushiguro] That
guy's incredible.

213
00:09:06,404 --> 00:09:08,821
He pulled off that shot
without using any cursed energy.

214
00:09:08,904 --> 00:09:11,194
I wonder if he's like Zen'in.

215
00:09:12,569 --> 00:09:15,028
Whoa! It's already
half past four!

216
00:09:15,111 --> 00:09:16,820
Later Coach! Got stuff to do!

217
00:09:16,903 --> 00:09:18,736
(hollers)

218
00:09:21,736 --> 00:09:23,987
(flashing)

219
00:09:24,069 --> 00:09:25,860
(gasp)

220
00:09:27,110 --> 00:09:28,735
The presence of a cursed object!

221
00:09:28,819 --> 00:09:29,610
Hey hold it!

222
00:09:29,694 --> 00:09:32,193
How is he that fast?

223
00:09:32,277 --> 00:09:34,735
I heard he can run the
50 meters in three seconds.

224
00:09:34,819 --> 00:09:35,819
Faster than my car!

225
00:09:35,902 --> 00:09:39,777
(gentle guitar music)

226
00:09:49,776 --> 00:09:50,859
I told you not to come!

227
00:09:50,943 --> 00:09:54,067
And stop bringing
flowers with you every time!

228
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:55,401
[Yuuji] You always say that.

229
00:09:55,484 --> 00:09:57,026
But you know
these aren't for you.

230
00:09:57,109 --> 00:09:58,233
They're for the nurses.

231
00:09:58,316 --> 00:09:59,817
All the more reason not to!

232
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:00,733
What's happening
with your school club?

233
00:10:00,817 --> 00:10:02,733
Why aren't you at your club?

234
00:10:02,817 --> 00:10:05,275
[Yuuji] Oh, chill out, Grandpa.

235
00:10:05,358 --> 00:10:07,316
The club meeting
was over hours ago.

236
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:10,066
If I didn't have extra time,
I wouldn't be visiting you.

237
00:10:10,149 --> 00:10:11,066
Good!

238
00:10:11,149 --> 00:10:13,857
Now, listen to me since
I've got free time too.

239
00:10:13,941 --> 00:10:15,899
[Yuuji] Not interested.

240
00:10:15,983 --> 00:10:17,857
Listen anyway, I've
got some things

241
00:10:17,941 --> 00:10:20,065
I want to say before
I reach the end.

242
00:10:20,148 --> 00:10:21,399
It's about your parents and

243
00:10:21,482 --> 00:10:22,065
-I want you to- -Come on!

244
00:10:22,148 --> 00:10:23,691
I told you, I'm not interested.

245
00:10:23,774 --> 00:10:26,649
Grandpa, please, could
you please stop trying to act

246
00:10:26,732 --> 00:10:27,941
all cool before you die?

247
00:10:28,024 --> 00:10:30,439
Every man has the
right to try to go out

248
00:10:30,523 --> 00:10:31,648
with a little style.

249
00:10:31,731 --> 00:10:33,011
Get a clue, you
useless grandson!

250
00:10:33,773 --> 00:10:35,773
Quit all your complaining.

251
00:10:35,856 --> 00:10:39,064
You don't have to
put on a show for me.

252
00:10:39,856 --> 00:10:40,773
(scoffs)

253
00:10:40,856 --> 00:10:43,064
You've had it too easy.

254
00:10:48,981 --> 00:10:50,939
Yuuji...

255
00:10:51,022 --> 00:10:52,563
[Yuuji] Hm?

256
00:10:52,647 --> 00:10:55,272
[Grandpa] You're a strong
kid, so try to help others.

257
00:10:55,355 --> 00:10:56,855
Save the people you can,

258
00:10:56,939 --> 00:10:58,981
even if it's only
those closest to you.

259
00:10:59,063 --> 00:11:00,248
It's okay if you lose your way,

260
00:11:00,272 --> 00:11:02,771
and don't worry about
whether they'll thank you or not.

261
00:11:02,854 --> 00:11:07,145
Just save as many as you can,
even if you can only save one.

262
00:11:08,562 --> 00:11:11,479
When you die, you should
be surrounded by people.

263
00:11:11,562 --> 00:11:12,771
Don't end up like me.

264
00:11:23,895 --> 00:11:26,311
[Yuuji] Grandpa?

265
00:11:26,395 --> 00:11:27,687
(phone beeping)

266
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:30,353
Yes? What can I do for you?

267
00:11:32,937 --> 00:11:34,143
Are you there?

268
00:11:34,227 --> 00:11:34,936
Mister Itadori!

269
00:11:35,019 --> 00:11:37,811
(sniffling)

270
00:11:37,894 --> 00:11:39,894
Hello, are you there?

271
00:11:41,769 --> 00:11:44,143
[Yuuji] My grandpa...

272
00:11:44,227 --> 00:11:45,227
is dead.

273
00:12:10,809 --> 00:12:13,809
There. That's all the
paperwork we need from you.

274
00:12:13,892 --> 00:12:15,850
[Yuuji] Yeah. Thanks
for helping me.

275
00:12:15,934 --> 00:12:19,017
Are you sure you're
going to be okay?

276
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:20,183
Well, I...

277
00:12:20,267 --> 00:12:24,808
I've never done this before
so it doesn't feel real yet.

278
00:12:24,891 --> 00:12:27,349
But then I know
Grandpa would snap at me

279
00:12:27,432 --> 00:12:28,872
if he saw me moping
around like this.

280
00:12:28,933 --> 00:12:32,182
So I'll just have to
laugh as I roast him!

281
00:12:32,266 --> 00:12:33,391
[Nurse] Be respectful.

282
00:12:35,891 --> 00:12:37,015
[Man] Yuuji Itadori?

283
00:12:37,098 --> 00:12:38,765
-Huh?
-Hm?

284
00:12:38,848 --> 00:12:41,223
I'm Fushiguro from Jujutsu Tech.

285
00:12:41,306 --> 00:12:43,807
I'd like to have a
word with you. Now.

286
00:12:43,890 --> 00:12:46,390
[Yuuji] Uh, I'm in
mourning right now.

287
00:12:46,473 --> 00:12:48,015
I understand,
but this can't wait.

288
00:12:48,098 --> 00:12:50,556
The cursed object you
possess is very dangerous.

289
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:52,223
I need you to hand it over.

290
00:12:52,306 --> 00:12:53,931
[Yuuji] Cursed object?

291
00:12:54,014 --> 00:12:54,889
[Fushiguro] This.

292
00:12:54,973 --> 00:12:58,014
Oh, yeah, that!
Yeah, I found that.

293
00:12:58,097 --> 00:13:00,430
I didn't think much of it.

294
00:13:00,514 --> 00:13:02,681
But my friends
were totally into it.

295
00:13:02,764 --> 00:13:03,847
What's dangerous about it?

296
00:13:05,472 --> 00:13:07,392
[Fushiguro] Every year
there are more than 10,000

297
00:13:07,472 --> 00:13:09,351
unexplained deaths and
missing persons in Japan.

298
00:13:12,013 --> 00:13:14,304
And most of those
are the result of curses.

299
00:13:15,054 --> 00:13:15,972
From curses?

300
00:13:16,054 --> 00:13:18,471
I don't care whether you
believe in them or not,

301
00:13:18,554 --> 00:13:20,263
the fact is they exist.

302
00:13:20,346 --> 00:13:21,846
Just listen.

303
00:13:21,930 --> 00:13:24,429
Large pools of negative
energy form easily

304
00:13:24,513 --> 00:13:27,220
in schools,
hospitals, and so on.

305
00:13:27,303 --> 00:13:29,595
Hardship, regret, shame.

306
00:13:29,679 --> 00:13:31,929
These emotions of mankind
become the source of curses.

307
00:13:32,012 --> 00:13:35,595
That's why most schools
secretly keep a cursed object

308
00:13:35,679 --> 00:13:37,428
to serve as a
protective talisman.

309
00:13:37,512 --> 00:13:39,595
Just like the one you
and your friends found.

310
00:13:39,679 --> 00:13:42,219
If it protects us, then
shouldn't we be grateful for it?

311
00:13:42,302 --> 00:13:43,528
[Fushiguro] Just let me finish!

312
00:13:43,552 --> 00:13:44,469
(grumbles)

313
00:13:44,552 --> 00:13:47,094
A cursed object needs
to be incredibly evil

314
00:13:47,177 --> 00:13:48,928
to keep lesser evil curses away.

315
00:13:49,011 --> 00:13:51,719
But its protection
isn't permanent.

316
00:13:53,511 --> 00:13:55,928
The problem is that their
seals weaken over time

317
00:13:56,011 --> 00:13:58,134
and then they serve
as a lure to attract

318
00:13:58,218 --> 00:13:59,885
and strengthen other curses.

319
00:13:59,969 --> 00:14:03,468
The object you found
is a dangerous one,

320
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:05,260
classified as special-grade.

321
00:14:05,343 --> 00:14:07,301
Now hand it over
before people start dying.

322
00:14:07,385 --> 00:14:10,510
Agh! I already told you
that I don't have it anymore.

323
00:14:10,593 --> 00:14:11,593
Here's the box.

324
00:14:13,550 --> 00:14:14,926
It's empty!

325
00:14:15,009 --> 00:14:18,133
I've just been following
a trace left by the object.

326
00:14:18,217 --> 00:14:19,300
Hold it!

327
00:14:19,384 --> 00:14:20,509
Where is it?

328
00:14:20,592 --> 00:14:21,425
Knock it off!

329
00:14:21,509 --> 00:14:22,902
You see Mm friends
were planning to...

330
00:14:22,926 --> 00:14:25,259
To do what?

331
00:14:25,342 --> 00:14:27,259
Well they were
saying let's open it up

332
00:14:27,342 --> 00:14:29,675
to see what's inside tonight.

333
00:14:29,758 --> 00:14:31,174
-Uh...
-(gasps)

334
00:14:31,258 --> 00:14:32,883
Why? Is that bad?

335
00:14:35,758 --> 00:14:37,132
It's way worse than bad.

336
00:14:38,383 --> 00:14:40,800
Your friends are going to die.

337
00:14:45,590 --> 00:14:46,715
I can't get it open.

338
00:14:46,799 --> 00:14:49,507
Did we really need to sneak
into the building for this?

339
00:14:49,590 --> 00:14:51,131
I'm gonna go turn on the light.

340
00:14:51,215 --> 00:14:53,173
No don't! We need
some atmosphere!

341
00:14:53,257 --> 00:14:56,173
Enjoying the thrill is
part of occult club isn't it?

342
00:14:56,257 --> 00:14:59,674
It's not like anything's
going to happen here anyway.

343
00:14:59,757 --> 00:15:00,798
(wrapping peels) (gasps)

344
00:15:00,881 --> 00:15:01,881
Hey!

345
00:15:13,798 --> 00:15:16,089
(mysterious music)

346
00:15:16,172 --> 00:15:18,546
[Iguchi] Whoa, a human finger!

347
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:19,630
Is it real?

348
00:15:20,046 --> 00:15:21,964
(gasps)

349
00:15:23,922 --> 00:15:24,838
You think...

350
00:15:24,922 --> 00:15:28,213
-(boom)
-(screams)

351
00:15:28,296 --> 00:15:29,338
What's going on?

352
00:15:29,421 --> 00:15:30,338
(voice trembling)

353
00:15:30,421 --> 00:15:32,629
(snarling)

354
00:15:33,921 --> 00:15:35,837
[Yuuji] Are talismans
that easy to open up?

355
00:15:35,921 --> 00:15:38,170
No, it's impossible for
those without cursed energy.

356
00:15:38,254 --> 00:15:39,170
Normally.

357
00:15:39,254 --> 00:15:40,170
(sighs)

358
00:15:40,254 --> 00:15:42,170
Go right here! Shortcut!

359
00:15:42,254 --> 00:15:45,379
[Fushiguro] This time the
object itself is too strong!

360
00:15:45,462 --> 00:15:48,836
And the seal is ancient. It
might as well be plain paper!

361
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:50,979
[Yuuji] I still don't get
all this stuff about curses!

362
00:15:51,003 --> 00:15:53,836
[Fushiguro] Is that the
building? Where are they?

363
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:55,378
Fourth floor!

364
00:15:55,461 --> 00:15:57,711
(grunts)

365
00:15:57,795 --> 00:15:58,378
(intense music)

366
00:15:58,461 --> 00:16:01,044
Whoa, what is this pressure?

367
00:16:01,127 --> 00:16:02,127
I'll handle this.

368
00:16:03,169 --> 00:16:06,377
Oh no way! I'm coming!

369
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:08,752
I may not know those
two that well, but...

370
00:16:08,835 --> 00:16:09,210
but they're friends!

371
00:16:09,293 --> 00:16:10,293
I have to help!

372
00:16:12,502 --> 00:16:13,877
You're staying here.

373
00:16:14,877 --> 00:16:17,252
(eerie music)

374
00:16:21,668 --> 00:16:24,209
(whimpering)

375
00:16:24,292 --> 00:16:26,584
(snarling)

376
00:16:28,251 --> 00:16:30,584
[Monster] What time is it?

377
00:16:32,251 --> 00:16:33,251
Just what is that thing?

378
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:36,208
[Iguchi] Sasaki?

379
00:16:36,291 --> 00:16:38,416
-(gasp)
-Oh, Iguchi! Thank goodness!

380
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:39,416
Where have you bee-

381
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:40,416
Help me!

382
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:41,416
(choking)

383
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:44,291
(voice trembling)

384
00:16:45,124 --> 00:16:47,458
What time is it?

385
00:16:47,541 --> 00:16:48,458
(screams)

386
00:16:48,541 --> 00:16:50,625
The curse has been unleashed!

387
00:16:50,708 --> 00:16:51,999
Its presence is everywhere!

388
00:16:52,082 --> 00:16:54,290
(panting)

389
00:16:54,374 --> 00:16:55,415
(snarling)

390
00:16:55,499 --> 00:16:56,707
Out of my way!

391
00:16:57,082 --> 00:16:57,999
Demon Dogs!

392
00:16:58,082 --> 00:17:01,624
(intense music)

393
00:17:02,791 --> 00:17:05,082
(howling)

394
00:17:05,165 --> 00:17:06,165
Eat it, boy!

395
00:17:08,706 --> 00:17:10,873
Am I really just
gonna sit here and wait

396
00:17:10,957 --> 00:17:11,957
because he told me to?

397
00:17:12,206 --> 00:17:14,039
What the hell am I so afraid of?

398
00:17:16,248 --> 00:17:18,122
Your friends are going to die.

399
00:17:18,206 --> 00:17:20,414
[Yuuji] He was right.

400
00:17:20,498 --> 00:17:22,248
I can sense death
all the way out here.

401
00:17:22,331 --> 00:17:24,956
I'm afraid of dying.

402
00:17:25,038 --> 00:17:26,664
Was I afraid of it before?

403
00:17:26,747 --> 00:17:28,038
It didn't feel like I was.

404
00:17:29,288 --> 00:17:31,038
I didn't cry because
I was scared.

405
00:17:31,372 --> 00:17:33,872
I just felt a little sad.

406
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:38,872
But my grandpa's death
and the death I'm facing now...

407
00:17:38,956 --> 00:17:40,079
How are they any different?

408
00:17:41,579 --> 00:17:43,659
[Grandpa] You're a strong
kid, so try to help others.

409
00:17:45,037 --> 00:17:46,496
(whimpering)

410
00:17:46,579 --> 00:17:48,871
(blasting)

411
00:17:50,204 --> 00:17:53,120
The curses are growing
in number! They're close!

412
00:17:55,120 --> 00:17:58,119
(snarling)

413
00:18:01,411 --> 00:18:02,411
There you are.

414
00:18:04,411 --> 00:18:07,328
[Yuuji] Grandpa was crabby,
short-tempered and stubborn!

415
00:18:07,411 --> 00:18:09,119
No one but me
ever even visited him!

416
00:18:09,203 --> 00:18:13,160
"Don't end up like me,"
huh? Well, no chance of that!

417
00:18:14,827 --> 00:18:15,994
[Fushiguro] Damn!

418
00:18:16,077 --> 00:18:18,369
Is it trying to swallow her
along with the cursed object?

419
00:18:18,452 --> 00:18:19,744
(moans)

420
00:18:19,827 --> 00:18:21,160
I'm not gonna make it!

421
00:18:21,244 --> 00:18:24,869
(dramatic music)

422
00:18:24,953 --> 00:18:27,368
(confused mumble)

423
00:18:27,451 --> 00:18:28,493
(glass shattering)

424
00:18:28,576 --> 00:18:30,868
(grunting)

425
00:18:30,952 --> 00:18:31,826
Itadori!!

426
00:18:31,910 --> 00:18:34,368
I think you had a
proper death, Grandpa!

427
00:18:35,284 --> 00:18:38,326
(grunting)

428
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:41,284
But this kind of a death...

429
00:18:43,408 --> 00:18:45,158
is just wrong!

430
00:18:45,242 --> 00:18:46,075
(snarling)

431
00:18:46,158 --> 00:18:49,784
(moaning)

432
00:18:49,867 --> 00:18:53,116
So this is a curse? Not
what I was expecting.

433
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:55,200
(groans)

434
00:18:57,450 --> 00:19:01,783
I should be asking what
you're doing here but good job.

435
00:19:01,866 --> 00:19:03,366
You're pretty smug, aren't you?

436
00:19:03,449 --> 00:19:05,908
So, just curious,

437
00:19:05,991 --> 00:19:07,824
what are those things
munching on the curse?

438
00:19:07,908 --> 00:19:10,908
My shikigami. Wait,
you can see them?

439
00:19:10,991 --> 00:19:12,699
Normally a curse can't be seen.

440
00:19:12,783 --> 00:19:14,574
Not unless you're
on the verge of death

441
00:19:14,658 --> 00:19:16,281
or in special places like this.

442
00:19:16,365 --> 00:19:17,990
Yeah, that makes sense.

443
00:19:18,073 --> 00:19:21,365
I've never seen ghosts or
weird stuff like this before.

444
00:19:21,448 --> 00:19:23,240
Huh. But you're
not scared though?

445
00:19:23,323 --> 00:19:26,782
I was. I mean for
a little while there.

446
00:19:26,865 --> 00:19:29,156
But then I thought,
everybody's gonna die.

447
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:31,239
Huh?

448
00:19:31,322 --> 00:19:33,280
So I want to make sure
that the people I know

449
00:19:33,364 --> 00:19:35,197
all have a chance
at a proper death.

450
00:19:37,197 --> 00:19:38,477
Not that I really understand it.

451
00:19:38,530 --> 00:19:39,447
Whoa!

452
00:19:39,530 --> 00:19:40,781
This it?

453
00:19:40,864 --> 00:19:44,364
Yeah, the cursed object,
Ryoumen Sukuna's finger.

454
00:19:44,447 --> 00:19:46,447
It's a miracle that
thing didn't swallow it.

455
00:19:46,530 --> 00:19:48,196
Why would anything
eat this? Is it good?

456
00:19:48,279 --> 00:19:50,154
Don't be dense.

457
00:19:50,238 --> 00:19:52,571
You'd eat it to gain
stronger cursed energy.

458
00:19:52,655 --> 00:19:55,071
Now hand it over,
it's dangerous.

459
00:19:55,154 --> 00:19:56,154
Fine, here.

460
00:19:57,488 --> 00:19:58,154
(gasps)

461
00:19:58,238 --> 00:20:01,071
(snarling)

462
00:20:01,154 --> 00:20:02,071
Run!

463
00:20:02,154 --> 00:20:03,987
(crash)

464
00:20:04,070 --> 00:20:06,946
(grunting)

465
00:20:07,028 --> 00:20:09,820
(electricity crackling)

466
00:20:09,904 --> 00:20:11,612
(growling)

467
00:20:11,695 --> 00:20:12,820
Damn!

468
00:20:12,904 --> 00:20:14,111
(growling)

469
00:20:14,195 --> 00:20:15,445
Nue!

470
00:20:15,528 --> 00:20:18,487
(grunting)

471
00:20:21,361 --> 00:20:22,486
(groaning)

472
00:20:22,569 --> 00:20:24,486
(roars)

473
00:20:24,569 --> 00:20:25,444
(blast)

474
00:20:25,527 --> 00:20:28,861
(dramatic music)

475
00:20:28,945 --> 00:20:30,236
(grunting)

476
00:20:32,736 --> 00:20:34,860
(roaring)

477
00:20:35,401 --> 00:20:37,652
Damn it!

478
00:20:37,735 --> 00:20:39,443
Why can't I think straight?

479
00:20:40,693 --> 00:20:41,777
Itadori!

480
00:20:41,860 --> 00:20:44,443
Your only chance is to
take those two and run for it!

481
00:20:44,526 --> 00:20:46,360
(roars)

482
00:20:46,443 --> 00:20:47,502
You're in big trouble yourself!

483
00:20:47,526 --> 00:20:50,443
(grunting)

484
00:20:51,275 --> 00:20:52,275
(yells)

485
00:20:52,359 --> 00:20:53,543
Only a curse can beat a curse!

486
00:20:53,567 --> 00:20:55,859
You cannot defeat this!

487
00:20:55,943 --> 00:20:57,359
Is that your idea of a pep talk?

488
00:20:57,442 --> 00:21:00,484
At this rate, we're
both gonna die!

489
00:21:02,108 --> 00:21:05,400
If I quit now I'll be having
this nightmare for weeks!

490
00:21:05,484 --> 00:21:06,484
Besides...

491
00:21:06,525 --> 00:21:08,733
(snarling)

492
00:21:09,775 --> 00:21:11,650
I know what I have to do!

493
00:21:11,733 --> 00:21:12,650
[Grandpa] Try to help others.

494
00:21:12,733 --> 00:21:15,858
I'm living with a rotten
curse of my own already!

495
00:21:16,441 --> 00:21:18,524
(grunts)

496
00:21:18,608 --> 00:21:20,358
(intense music)

497
00:21:26,398 --> 00:21:30,023
You idiot! Throw it down to
me or you'll both get eaten!

498
00:21:30,106 --> 00:21:31,523
(grunting)

499
00:21:31,607 --> 00:21:33,398
(growling)

500
00:21:33,482 --> 00:21:36,440
[Yuuji] Why would
anything eat this? Is it good?

501
00:21:36,523 --> 00:21:37,732
[Fushiguro] Don't be dense.

502
00:21:37,815 --> 00:21:39,689
You'd eat it to gain
stronger cursed energy.

503
00:21:39,773 --> 00:21:42,731
(straining)

504
00:21:42,814 --> 00:21:45,064
There's a way I
can save everyone!

505
00:21:45,147 --> 00:21:48,898
I just need to have my
own cursed energy. don't I?

506
00:21:48,981 --> 00:21:50,314
Don't do it.

507
00:21:50,397 --> 00:21:51,564
Don't do it!

508
00:21:51,648 --> 00:21:52,522
(swallowing)

509
00:21:52,606 --> 00:21:54,521
Ryoumen Sukuna's finger!

510
00:21:54,605 --> 00:21:56,313
That's a special-grade
cursed object!

511
00:21:56,396 --> 00:21:59,563
It's a deadly poison!
He'll die for sure!

512
00:22:01,230 --> 00:22:04,188
But, there is a chance, a
one-in-a-million chance

513
00:22:04,271 --> 00:22:05,980
(boom)

514
00:22:06,063 --> 00:22:08,104
(grunts)

515
00:22:09,355 --> 00:22:11,896
(roaring)

516
00:22:11,979 --> 00:22:13,896
(blast)

517
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:21,812
(gasp)

518
00:22:33,811 --> 00:22:36,019
(cackling)

519
00:22:44,852 --> 00:22:48,393
[Yuuji] I knew it! The
light feels best in the flesh!

520
00:22:48,477 --> 00:22:51,727
[Fushiguro] This is the worst,
a one-in-a-million-chance,

521
00:22:51,810 --> 00:22:52,936
worst-case scenario!

522
00:22:53,018 --> 00:22:55,727
The special-grade cursed
object has incarnated!

523
00:22:55,810 --> 00:22:57,977
Cursed flesh is so boring!

524
00:22:58,060 --> 00:23:00,434
So now where are the
people? The women?

525
00:23:03,226 --> 00:23:05,976
What a wonderful
era to be reawakened!

526
00:23:06,059 --> 00:23:09,142
Women and children are
crawling everywhere like maggots!

527
00:23:09,226 --> 00:23:10,476
How marvelous!

528
00:23:10,559 --> 00:23:13,017
It'll be a massacre!

529
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:14,558
(cackling)

530
00:23:14,642 --> 00:23:17,767
(confused mumbling)

531
00:23:17,850 --> 00:23:20,266
[Yuuji] What do you think
you're doing with my body?

532
00:23:20,350 --> 00:23:21,350
Give it back!

533
00:23:21,725 --> 00:23:24,266
Hey, wait. How
are you doing that?

534
00:23:24,350 --> 00:23:26,808
Well, it's my body!

535
00:23:26,892 --> 00:23:28,266
Wait...

536
00:23:28,350 --> 00:23:29,600
He's suppressing me?

537
00:23:29,683 --> 00:23:32,182
[Fushiguro] Stay
right where you are!

538
00:23:32,265 --> 00:23:33,766
You're no longer human!

539
00:23:33,849 --> 00:23:34,849
Huh?

540
00:23:35,557 --> 00:23:38,140
Under Jujutsu regulation....

541
00:23:38,224 --> 00:23:39,849
Yuuji Itadori...

542
00:23:39,933 --> 00:23:42,474
by law I will now
exorcize you...

543
00:23:42,557 --> 00:23:43,557
as a curse!

544
00:23:45,474 --> 00:23:47,431
(dramatic music)

